# No em dashes

- Never use em dashes in website copy, documentation, comments, commit messages, or responses about this project.
- Use a period, comma, colon, parentheses, or a rewritten sentence instead. Do not substitute double hyphens as punctuation.
- Apply this rule to all new and edited text, including copy carried forward from earlier suggestions.
- Preserve exact external quotations or machine-required syntax when changing punctuation would alter their meaning or behavior.
